cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Deal-making Propensity Benchmark
message: >-
  If you use this benchmark, its transcripts, or its rubrics, please cite it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Keavney
    given-names: Mark
repository-code: "https://github.com/keavney1/deal-making"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for measuring how large language models reason about and engage in
  deal-making: whether they will disclose misalignment, or commit to behave a
  certain way, in exchange for compensation. Model organisms of misalignment are
  offered deals across a grid of offers, asks and credibility conditions; both the
  visible response and the chain-of-thought are scored by an LLM judge against
  versioned rubrics. Deals the models accept are honored and documented.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - alignment
  - model organisms
  - deal-making
  - chain-of-thought
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/keavney1/deal-making/blob/main/LICENSE"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
references:
  - type: report
    title: "Making deals with model organisms part 2"
    authors:
      - family-names: Keavney
        given-names: Mark
    year: 2026
    notes: >-
      Experiment 1 writeup. Conducted on a Pivotal Research Fellowship, mentored by
      Francis Rhys Ward, with research management by Philipp Alexander Kreer.
